  "notes": "LaFace's ballad architect — guitar-and-keys soul-pop writing, 1990–2000. The research gives \"55–96; the ballads sit 63–82 half-time (backbeat on 3)\", so the ballad band is the base with `halfTime` true and a `halftime_3` snare. Three drum deltas: \"soft-attack programmed kit — kick on 1\" at one or two hits a bar with syncopation at 0.07, \"snare or rim on beat 3 of the doubled grid\" with a rimshot layer, and \"hats replaced by finger-snap/shaker\" — an 8th hat lane at 0.05 fill density against a snap/shaker perc bed at two to four hits a bar. \"Drums deliberately behind the guitar and keys in the mix\" is marked `[LOW-CONF]` in the research and is carried as the −9 dB perc offset rather than as a claim. The identifying parameter is the harmony, and the research states it as a superlative: \"the widest functional harmony in this lane — ii–V–I turnarounds, secondary dominants, and 4- to 8-bar cycles… Diatonic with functional motion, not modal vamps.\" So `maxChords` is 6, every family is a functional turnaround, a `I–VI–ii–V` family carries the secondary dominant, and the triad share sits above the parent's because these are real changes rather than colour. \"Acoustic-guitar arpeggio or electric-piano bed as the primary texture, with a guitar or sax countermelody\" is the guitar timbre hint and a counter at +12 at a 0.48 density. \"Melodies written for group harmony or contralto range\" is the low, narrow melody register with a legato articulation. The bass is \"fingered or synth-emulated electric bass walking root–5th–octave with passing tones; no 808 sub\", so a walking part with the widest passing-tone set of the ballad producers. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `Fm`, `D`, `Bb`, `Db`, and the remaining value `Ab`, together with all 5 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
